{
 "comment": "Trees and bushes of the terrain core (the 'trees' module; the grass cover is its own module, terrain_core::Grass). `models`: source model and texture inside the unpacked new_assets archives (.cache/foliage_src), built by tools/terrain_lab/build_foliage.py into assets/terrain_core/foliage. `layers`: what is scattered together - one candidate per `spacing_m` cell out to `range_m` from the eye, one of `models` by hash, scaled within `scale`, nowhere steeper than `min_normal_z`; Heavy models belong in short-range layers (`saplings`, 300+ triangles, out to 400 m), cheap cards in the long ones (trees, 52 triangles, to 3.5 km). `max_count` caps the instances one frame may draw. `biomes`: per biome id (content/config/biomes/fallen_gods.json) and layer, [density - the chance a candidate is placed; cluster_m - size of the noise patches it grows in, 0 for evenly; cover - the share of the ground those patches cover]. The great marshes (1) grow nothing but grass and moss; their edge by the dark forest (17, biomes.json bands) has the forest closing in (broadleaf stands in for the marshes' gnarled trees until those exist). The stele's glade (18, tools/terrain_lab/stele_glade.py) has only dead trees, here and there: crooked bare trunks with broken limbs made by tools/blender/dead_trees.py (assets/source/dead_trees).",
